# Generation 3, round 3, W-07 (generations/gen003/PLAN.md, version 3, the wide screen). Wick absorption.
# For each hourly bar, (open + close - high - low) / close = (lower wick - upper wick) / close: positive when the bar's
# lower wick is longer (selling pushed the price down and was absorbed within the hour), negative when the upper wick
# is longer; it does not depend on the direction of the bar's body. z = its mean over the last m weekly bins divided
# by the mean hourly range (high - low) / close over the same bins: the net absorption per unit of range. Weekly bins
# visible at the bar that opens Sunday 23:00, traded at the Monday 00:00 open. Long the most net lower wick, short the
# most net upper wick; rank weights, dollar neutral, gross 1. No funding, mark or index input.
name = "gen003_w07_wick_absorption"
family = "other"
kind = "portfolio"
unit = "top30"
hypothesis = "Absorption: a lower wick means aggressive selling met resting bids that absorbed it; when that repeats through the weeks a patient large buyer is accumulating, and its demand persists, while repeated upper wicks mark passive distribution. Long the coins with the most net lower-wick absorption per unit of range over the last m weeks, short the most net upper wick, weekly. Falsified if the DEV screen fails, VAL PSR(0) < 0.90, 2x costs negative, no G6 timing, or next30 disagrees."

m = param(2, 1, 3)             # weekly bins averaged (2 weeks)

w = (open + close - high - low) / close
g = (high - low) / close
z = sma(tf_mean(w, weekly), m) / sma(tf_mean(g, weekly), m)
signal = cs_scale(cs_demean(cs_rank(z)))
